WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:05.100
Being on SCP-173 detail isn’t easy.

00:00:05.100 --> 00:00:11.240
These duties of strict observation fall on
a bi-weekly basis when SCP-173’s enclosure

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.589
needs to be cleaned.

00:00:12.589 --> 00:00:18.220
The reddish-brown substance on the floor is
a natural output of SCP-173, a combination

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.680
of feces and blood.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.520
While the Foundation has put up with a lot
of depraved behavior from its SCPs, it draws

00:00:24.520 --> 00:00:26.310
the line at poor hygiene.

00:00:26.310 --> 00:00:30.910
They routinely send in a crew of three D class
personnel to clean up the mess.

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:35.570
But the bigger chore isn’t the scrubbing
and mopping at all, but rather keeping SCP-173

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:36.570
docile.

00:00:36.570 --> 00:00:43.260
To do so, the line of sight must not be broken
at any time with SCP-173.

00:00:43.260 --> 00:00:47.090
Personnel assigned to enter the container
are instructed to alert one another before

00:00:47.090 --> 00:00:48.090
blinking.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:53.590
If this protocol is not followed, SCP-173
attacks by snapping the neck at the base of

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:54.590
the skull.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:58.880
It is, at its core, a high-stakes staring
contest.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.410
The crew is intelligently divided into their
tasks.

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:05.640
Only one of them actually has janitorial duties.

00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.640
And even then, the mopper’s most relevant
skill isn’t even related to cleaning at

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.640
all.

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:13.970
His greatest strength must be his ability
to trust other people.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:19.060
As he takes his mop to the floor, he hands
over his life to his crew, who protect him

00:01:19.060 --> 00:01:23.479
with their focus and attention on SCP-173.

00:01:23.479 --> 00:01:27.780
It is without a doubt one of the cruelest
and most stressful jobs anyone could ever

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:28.780
have.

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.500
But not every horror story is found in the
trenches of terror.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:37.250
Those with mops on the frontlines have their
work cut out for them, but even the researchers

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:43.200
with their warm lab coats and boring bureaucratic
obligations aren’t safe from danger.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:49.020
This is the story of Jake Scholl, a researcher
who - for reasons we will tactfully tease

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:55.110
you with until the video's witty end - had
been reassigned to SCP-173.

00:01:55.110 --> 00:01:57.940
Director Fordham brought the bad news like
a bag of coal.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:03.200
"You're being reassigned," he said, with a
slight smirk on his face, continuing to be

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:08.479
preoccupied with his paperwork, as if this
news was secondary to what he was doing right

00:02:08.479 --> 00:02:09.810
there and then.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.200
But it wasn’t secondary to Jack Scholl.

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:14.430
It was the center of their life.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:15.430
No.

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.900
Not even just the center.

00:02:16.900 --> 00:02:22.380
It was the center, peripheral, and outer bounds
of their life.

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.010
Their assignments were everything.

00:02:24.010 --> 00:02:26.910
And everything was about to change.

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:30.120
A pregnant silence followed the announcement.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:34.980
Jake Scholl couldn’t find a response, and
they weren't even sure there was one to be

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:37.560
found, no matter how deep they dug.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.370
What came out wasn’t as much of a retort
as a reaction.

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:45.260
That involuntary bodily response to events
that weren’t expected.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:49.460
That awkward and afraid muttering of fear
and confusion.

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:50.460
"I—.

00:02:50.460 --> 00:02:51.460
What?

00:02:51.460 --> 00:02:53.320
I'm being…

00:02:53.320 --> 00:02:54.320
what?

00:02:54.320 --> 00:02:55.320
I’m…

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:56.320
I’m…

00:02:56.320 --> 00:02:59.319
I’m to be reassigned.

00:02:59.319 --> 00:03:00.750
Is that what you’re saying?"

00:03:00.750 --> 00:03:03.430
Researcher Scholl blinked a few times, confused.

00:03:03.430 --> 00:03:07.300
Their feet sunk into the deep forest green
shag on the floor.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:11.620
A spectrum of thoughts cascaded through their
mind, as they searched harder and harder for

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.620
reason.

00:03:12.620 --> 00:03:17.980
Digger deeper and deeper only to find another
treasure chest full of nothing.

00:03:17.980 --> 00:03:21.710
"Is my work…not sufficient on SCP—"

00:03:21.710 --> 00:03:26.159
Director Fordham looked up, and gave them
the fixed, pointed stare they’d grown to

00:03:26.159 --> 00:03:28.580
dread over the past six months.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:30.489
"Of course not, Jake.

00:03:30.489 --> 00:03:35.840
I recognize what you've done, and we want
to put you somewhere I feel you deserve.

00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.000
And serve the Foundation, of course.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:41.879
We're putting you on a very important, and
special, object."

00:03:41.879 --> 00:03:44.459
Again, Fordham gave that smirk.

00:03:44.459 --> 00:03:45.959
That damn smirk.

00:03:45.959 --> 00:03:51.930
Sure, his words and tone presented themselves
as the truth, but his face said otherwise.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:57.400
The devious positioning of his lip suggested
there was a layer of sinister subtext to his

00:03:57.400 --> 00:03:58.400
speech.

00:03:58.400 --> 00:03:59.849
But Jake Scholl couldn’t pick up on the
cues.

00:03:59.849 --> 00:04:04.420
There is no room to read someone else’s
poker face when all of your attention is on

00:04:04.420 --> 00:04:06.660
the crappy hand you’ve just been dealt.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.900
Jake Scholl's eyes fell to the desk.

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:10.900
Reassigned.

00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:12.900
The word rang like church bells.

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:14.050
Why god!?

00:04:14.050 --> 00:04:19.829
Their work with SCP-3872 as a consulting chemist
was going slowly, to be truthful, but they

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:23.490
didn't think it was to the point that they
needed reassignment.

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:25.169
"A-Alright.

00:04:25.169 --> 00:04:27.349
Which project am I assigned to?"

00:04:27.349 --> 00:04:31.199
The time between the question and the answer
was the longest of Jake’s life.

00:04:31.199 --> 00:04:33.680
The uncertainty felt like an eternity.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:39.490
Fordham tapped a few symbols accessing Scholl's
profile, and added an entry in their security

00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:40.490
clearance.

00:04:40.490 --> 00:04:44.830
He hastily swiped away all the other files
listed and turned back to face Scholl.

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:46.659
"You have access to it now.

00:04:46.659 --> 00:04:49.120
Please get on the first plane to Site-19.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:51.869
Your dormitory contents are already packed
up."

00:04:51.869 --> 00:04:55.830
Jake reached into their pocket to check the
notifications on their cell phone.

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:58.020
[SCP-DB NOTIFICATION] &gt; SCP-3872.

00:04:58.020 --> 00:04:59.039
FILE REMOVED.

00:04:59.039 --> 00:05:01.490
[SCP-DB NOTIFICATION] &gt; SCP-2593.

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:02.520
FILE REMOVED.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:05.639
[SCP-DB NOTIFICATION] &gt; SCP-173.

00:05:05.639 --> 00:05:06.639
FILE ADDED.

00:05:06.639 --> 00:05:11.099
They turned around, and walked slowly through
the corridors, towards the transportation

00:05:11.099 --> 00:05:12.949
hub on the outskirts of the site.

00:05:12.949 --> 00:05:18.139
They opened the file on their phone, and quickly
scanned the oddly phrased report, attempting

00:05:18.139 --> 00:05:20.309
to make sense of what they were reading.

00:05:20.309 --> 00:05:25.800
Scholl's eyebrows raised to the heavens as
they noticed the timestamp on containment.

00:05:25.800 --> 00:05:28.210
SCP-173 was one of the first.

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:32.139
One of the few objects that the Foundation
came to possess through some organization

00:05:32.139 --> 00:05:35.319
or another, without losing its information.

00:05:35.319 --> 00:05:39.919
They tried their best to remain optimistic
in their interpretation of these new life

00:05:39.919 --> 00:05:40.969
events.

00:05:40.969 --> 00:05:45.139
And for a moment, they thought, “This might
be a good thing for me.”

00:05:45.139 --> 00:05:49.240
Swiping down, they came to the section about
assigned researchers, the people whose steps

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.339
they would be following in.

00:05:50.339 --> 00:05:53.159
And where were those steps leading them?

00:05:53.159 --> 00:05:57.560
The list was impressive, from Dr. Kondraki
to Dr. Bright.

00:05:57.560 --> 00:05:59.979
These people were all legends in their own
right.

00:05:59.979 --> 00:06:04.599
And so if they could just follow their footsteps,
they reasoned they would end their journey

00:06:04.599 --> 00:06:05.939
in a good place.

00:06:05.939 --> 00:06:10.779
They imagined their new career path straight
to the top of the mountain of success.

00:06:10.779 --> 00:06:11.779
Maybe they would make groundbreaking discoveries.

00:06:11.779 --> 00:06:13.770
Maybe they would become the face of the Foundation.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:18.309
Maybe they would accomplish so much that there’d
be a statue erected in their honor that people

00:06:18.309 --> 00:06:21.929
travel far and wide to visit and take pictures
with.

00:06:21.929 --> 00:06:24.800
Maybe this would be a good thing, they wanted
to think.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:28.660
"I need the first plane to Site-19,” they
said with confidence.

00:06:28.660 --> 00:06:30.349
“I've been reassigned."

00:06:30.349 --> 00:06:34.800
And so, Jake Scholl took to the air and clung
to this dream as long as they could.

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:40.210
But no matter how heavy a sleeper, reality
shakes everyone awake eventually.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.419
Six years later.

00:06:42.419 --> 00:06:44.419
Jake Scholl could hear the years pass.

00:06:44.419 --> 00:06:47.899
But not only could they hear it, they could
feel it.

00:06:47.899 --> 00:06:53.249
Their body was decaying in a way inconsistent
with our biological understanding of age.

00:06:53.249 --> 00:06:54.449
SCP-173.

00:06:54.449 --> 00:06:56.969
The legendary object.

00:06:56.969 --> 00:07:00.429
The first, the original, the Statue.

00:07:00.429 --> 00:07:03.409
It was chipping away at the soul of Jake Scholl.

00:07:03.409 --> 00:07:06.169
It was carving a statue of its own.

00:07:06.169 --> 00:07:08.539
Hacking at stone until it was nothing.

00:07:08.539 --> 00:07:11.389
And that’s what Jake Scholl felt like.

00:07:11.389 --> 00:07:12.389
Nothing.

00:07:12.389 --> 00:07:13.389
It was torture.

00:07:13.389 --> 00:07:17.240
When they arrived, they quickly reviewed the
research materials.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:20.360
Every word had become burned into their memory.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:21.749
All 233 words of them.

00:07:21.749 --> 00:07:28.009
The "additional research materials" turned
out to be a few scribbled pages by bored researchers.

00:07:28.009 --> 00:07:32.270
A few had made hypotheses that had all turned
out to be nonsense.

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:37.229
There was a locked filing cabinet, but every
time Scholl requested it be opened, maintenance

00:07:37.229 --> 00:07:43.060
told them that the control room was designated
"low priority" and they would get to it eventually.

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:47.919
Over the past six years, Jake Scholl had made
18 separate transfer requests.

00:07:47.919 --> 00:07:49.229
They wanted out.

00:07:49.229 --> 00:07:51.039
But all of them had been denied.

00:07:51.039 --> 00:07:53.520
It was as if they were in high school again.

00:07:53.520 --> 00:07:58.279
Asking dates to prom and getting hit with
no thank you’s, feeling none of the politeness

00:07:58.279 --> 00:08:04.580
baked into their syntax, understanding only
the brute reality of the phrase: “No.”

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:09.629
They were stuck here, technically a Level
3 staff now, but without any rights to view

00:08:09.629 --> 00:08:12.029
or work on any other objects.

00:08:12.029 --> 00:08:16.819
They were given a promotion but it withheld
all the perks and benefits that come with

00:08:16.819 --> 00:08:17.819
it.

00:08:17.819 --> 00:08:20.619
They were stuck in a loop of pats on the back.

00:08:20.619 --> 00:08:25.449
People extended them their hand, but it was
always with an empty palm… giving them nothing

00:08:25.449 --> 00:08:28.020
to hold onto but a gesture.

00:08:28.020 --> 00:08:29.949
They were assigned a staff of four.

00:08:29.949 --> 00:08:36.190
Three D-class, all of which were older men,
and a lazy level 2 Security Officer, who slouched

00:08:36.190 --> 00:08:41.560
in his office chair, meeting the bare minimum
requirements to be considered a living human

00:08:41.560 --> 00:08:42.560
being.

00:08:42.560 --> 00:08:44.310
The D-class were all quite docile.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:49.019
They came in once a week, mopped the floor,
mumbled "Clear '' to each other, and left.

00:08:49.019 --> 00:08:51.529
They lived within this exact structure.

00:08:51.529 --> 00:08:55.310
“No new days,” became an unspoken motto.

00:08:55.310 --> 00:08:58.110
These recurring 24 hours passed slowly.

00:08:58.110 --> 00:09:02.750
If there were no clocks to prove the passing
of time, they would have every reason to believe

00:09:02.750 --> 00:09:04.740
it had frozen over.

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:09.660
But occasionally, ever so occasionally, the
day would deviate just slightly.

00:09:09.660 --> 00:09:11.000
They’d hear something.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:13.940
A scrape and the sounds of movement.

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:19.250
Jake would flip open the observation ports
on the double-concrete lock and examine SCP-173.

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:23.139
But Jake could take offense to such language.

00:09:23.139 --> 00:09:25.350
Examining might be the wrong word.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:27.629
More accurately, they would just look at it.

00:09:27.629 --> 00:09:29.769
Because there was nothing to examine.

00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:31.940
There was nothing to observe.

00:09:31.940 --> 00:09:34.829
SCP-173 was already understood.

00:09:34.829 --> 00:09:39.860
Michael Jordan doesn’t take a microscope
to the ball every time he plans to dribble.

00:09:39.860 --> 00:09:42.270
He knows every detail of it by heart.

00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.389
His fingertips know the grooves.

00:09:44.389 --> 00:09:47.079
His hand-eye coordination knows how to control
it.

00:09:47.079 --> 00:09:51.709
His right arm’s built-in apt for physics
knows exactly how much force to put into each

00:09:51.709 --> 00:09:54.180
shot and at what trajectory to aim.

00:09:54.180 --> 00:09:59.700
We are told to learn something new every day,
but the truth is, there comes a day when the

00:09:59.700 --> 00:10:00.949
learning stops.

00:10:00.949 --> 00:10:03.160
When we know all that we will ever know.

00:10:03.160 --> 00:10:05.290
And this felt true to Jake.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.990
They understood SCP-173.

00:10:07.990 --> 00:10:09.850
There was nothing more for them to see.

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:13.389
It was just concrete, rebar, and some spray
paint.

00:10:13.389 --> 00:10:14.600
That was it.

00:10:14.600 --> 00:10:16.910
And that was all that it would ever be.

00:10:16.910 --> 00:10:20.110
There was nothing to find, nothing to determine.

00:10:20.110 --> 00:10:22.430
Nothing for the researcher to research.

00:10:22.430 --> 00:10:26.000
Their job was done, but they kept having to
work it.

00:10:26.000 --> 00:10:31.370
Their identity no longer fit, but they kept
having to put it on each and every morning.

00:10:31.370 --> 00:10:35.790
When Jake first got there, they collected
samples of the concrete, some of the rebar,

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:36.890
some spray paint.

00:10:36.890 --> 00:10:40.519
They were determined to find something worthy
of research.

00:10:40.519 --> 00:10:45.019
After four weeks, they’d gotten sick of
getting no replies from admin, and they cracked

00:10:45.019 --> 00:10:50.759
the lock on the filing cabinet, finding the
research notes of all the previous researchers.

00:10:50.759 --> 00:10:55.440
All of the "legendary" doctors' notes turned
out to be doodles and random to-do lists which

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:57.519
had nothing to do with the object.

00:10:57.519 --> 00:11:00.670
After six weeks they gave up on taking samples.

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:02.930
After eight weeks, they brought a Gameboy.

00:11:02.930 --> 00:11:08.710
After ten, they started bringing in anything
they could to pass the time: a yoyo, a collection

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:13.970
of short stories, a packet of hot sauce they
felt bad throwing away, a piece of string

00:11:13.970 --> 00:11:18.190
to cut off circulation to their index finger
for no other reason than to make sure they

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.440
were still a human relying on blood.

00:11:20.440 --> 00:11:24.019
Oh yes, Jake Scholl was bored.

00:11:24.019 --> 00:11:26.240
So very bored.

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:31.980
They thought if anyone could bring the phrase
BORED TO DEATH to fruition, it would be them.

00:11:31.980 --> 00:11:35.990
These days, they shuffled in, waved at the
guard, and sat down at the little control

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:41.680
room where there was a terminal, which didn't
have an internet connection, and tried to

00:11:41.680 --> 00:11:43.079
stay sane.

00:11:43.079 --> 00:11:46.459
Fast forward a few years and Jake barely fit
into his chair.

00:11:46.459 --> 00:11:50.140
To clarify, no, they did not purchase a new,
tiny chair out of boredom.

00:11:50.140 --> 00:11:52.540
They got fat out of boredom.

00:11:52.540 --> 00:11:57.689
Their life brought them no joy, and so what
they couldn’t get from living, they searched

00:11:57.689 --> 00:11:59.339
for in eating.

00:11:59.339 --> 00:12:03.550
But there was no fulfillment to be found at
the center of the tootsie pop.

00:12:03.550 --> 00:12:07.850
Jake stood with a grunt, as the light came
on, and the three D-class were escorted to

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:11.130
the control room, with the mops and buckets
in tow.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:15.459
"Thanks, Jimmy,” was the only conversation
they had with the new security staff.

00:12:15.459 --> 00:12:18.680
The old guard had retired sometime in the
eighth year.

00:12:18.680 --> 00:12:20.259
Honestly, Jake couldn't even remember.

00:12:20.259 --> 00:12:25.240
The D-class had gotten older too, most of
them now gray-haired, but still assigned to

00:12:25.240 --> 00:12:26.250
the project.

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:29.319
The security guard walked over and thumbed
towards the break room.

00:12:29.319 --> 00:12:31.420
"Hey Jake, I'm going to get coffee.

00:12:31.420 --> 00:12:33.730
If anything happens, seal the door, you know
the drill.

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.899
Just keep an eye on the D's."

00:12:35.899 --> 00:12:39.839
Jake buzzed the doors open and stood inside
the door frame, keeping their eyes on the

00:12:39.839 --> 00:12:43.759
statue most of the time, but wandering over
the containment chamber.

00:12:43.759 --> 00:12:48.310
A long time ago, they might have been concerned,
but the D-classes they worked with weren't

00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:49.310
violent.

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:53.850
Frankly, they had worked with these men long
enough that they extended a small measure

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:55.029
of trust.

00:12:55.029 --> 00:12:59.939
All of them did their jobs without complaining
and had never made a mistake in ten years.

00:12:59.939 --> 00:13:05.560
While the years of repetition wore them out,
the job itself didn’t even feel like labor.

00:13:05.560 --> 00:13:08.690
They had perfected the art of the staring
contest.

00:13:08.690 --> 00:13:11.850
They were confident, and they had reason to
be.

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:18.430
As the years went on, although they collected
no new data on SCP-173, they did collect evidence.

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:21.110
Evidence that they were capable of containing
it.

00:13:21.110 --> 00:13:27.470
While they learned nothing of importance about
SCP-173, they learned about themselves.

00:13:27.470 --> 00:13:29.149
They learned that they were a good crew.

00:13:29.149 --> 00:13:34.779
And it was because of this confidence, even
if rightfully earned, that success crumbled.

00:13:34.779 --> 00:13:40.829
When in a room with SCP-173 you have to assume
everything will go wrong.

00:13:40.829 --> 00:13:43.639
Because anything can go wrong.

00:13:43.639 --> 00:13:45.709
And eventually, it will.

00:13:45.709 --> 00:13:49.389
And when that time comes, you have to be prepared.

00:13:49.389 --> 00:13:53.980
Procedure said Jake had to have someone armed
in the room with any D-class.

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:57.529
Jake looked down at their hip, double-checking
the pistol there.

00:13:57.529 --> 00:14:00.870
They knew how to use it but figured he never
would have to draw it.

00:14:00.870 --> 00:14:02.540
The routine cleaning began.

00:14:02.540 --> 00:14:03.540
"Clear."

00:14:03.540 --> 00:14:04.540
"Clear."

00:14:04.540 --> 00:14:05.540
"Clear."

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:07.529
It was the same old, same old.

00:14:07.529 --> 00:14:08.529
Until…suddenly…

00:14:08.529 --> 00:14:09.529
it wasn’t.

00:14:09.529 --> 00:14:10.529
"Cl..

00:14:10.529 --> 00:14:12.910
Cl… oh no, I think I'm having a—…" SNAP

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:15.580
"What, hey Nick, are you—" SNAP

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:18.749
"Oh god, no I don't wanna—" SNAP

00:14:18.749 --> 00:14:22.240
Jake's eyes shot up, as the Statue stood inches
away.

00:14:22.240 --> 00:14:25.259
Its green eyes stared directly into their
soul.

00:14:25.259 --> 00:14:30.660
In their periphery, Jake could see the three
D-class with their heads turned at odd angles.

00:14:30.660 --> 00:14:34.220
Jake desperately reached out for the emergency
containment button on the wall.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:38.759
They hadn’t ever had to use it, and it was
supposed to be easy to find.

00:14:38.759 --> 00:14:40.410
But of course, it wasn’t.

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:45.029
They recalled the manual saying, “Move your
hand anywhere along the right-hand wall, the

00:14:45.029 --> 00:14:46.579
button takes up most of the wall.

00:14:46.579 --> 00:14:52.110
It will seal off the containment chamber,
and SCP-173 from breaching containment.”

00:14:52.110 --> 00:14:56.209
They moved their hand exactly how their memory
of the manual instructed him.

00:14:56.209 --> 00:14:57.480
But it wasn't there.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:59.120
There was nothing to press.

00:14:59.120 --> 00:15:01.279
There was nothing to save them.

00:15:01.279 --> 00:15:04.610
Jake's hands grew desperate, and their eyes
began to water.

00:15:04.610 --> 00:15:08.569
Just as they started to close, a last thought
crossed their mind.

00:15:08.569 --> 00:15:13.730
Move your hand anywhere along the left hand
wall, the button takes up most of the wall.

00:15:13.730 --> 00:15:19.459
It will seal off the containment chamber,
and SCP-173 from breaching containment.

00:15:19.459 --> 00:15:21.309
Of course, a classic mix-up.

00:15:21.309 --> 00:15:24.529
Fifty-fifty chances never favor the flustered.

00:15:24.529 --> 00:15:27.589
Their fight or flight instincts were contradicting
each other.

00:15:27.589 --> 00:15:30.660
Was reaching for a button fighting or was
it flighting?

00:15:30.660 --> 00:15:32.000
They were in their head.

00:15:32.000 --> 00:15:33.470
Deep in trenches of overthinking.

00:15:33.470 --> 00:15:35.869
Finally, they regained their composure.

00:15:35.869 --> 00:15:39.680
Their hand darted out to the left, and they
started to push down on the button.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:44.640
The red of the emergency button filled their
vision, as the green eyes of SCP-173 slipped

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.399
just barely out of…

00:15:46.399 --> 00:15:47.399
SNAP!

00:15:47.399 --> 00:15:50.959
Director Kingsley stood outside of the meeting
room, a few minutes before the weekly briefing

00:15:50.959 --> 00:15:53.740
in the Site-217 administrative wing.

00:15:53.740 --> 00:15:54.820
"Fordham.

00:15:54.820 --> 00:15:56.170
Do you remember Jake Scholl?"

00:15:56.170 --> 00:15:57.170
"Sure do."

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:59.519
"Just got a report from 19.

00:15:59.519 --> 00:16:01.550
Looks like there was a breach, and they bit
it."

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:04.730
Fordham waved off a few colleagues who were
about to enter the meeting room.

00:16:04.730 --> 00:16:07.329
His conversation with Director Kingsley wasn’t
over.

00:16:07.329 --> 00:16:11.790
He went on to tell him that he was just about
to approve Jake Sholl’s transfer.

00:16:11.790 --> 00:16:17.130
After all these years Jake had been sending
requests to leave SCP-173, their wish was

00:16:17.130 --> 00:16:18.240
about to be granted.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.800
But instead, they were reassigned to the grave.

00:16:20.800 --> 00:16:23.019
What a cruel twist, isn’t it?

00:16:23.019 --> 00:16:26.019
That is, of course, if it were actually true.

00:16:26.019 --> 00:16:28.709
Fordham gave his patented smirk.

00:16:28.709 --> 00:16:30.270
“Just kidding.

00:16:30.270 --> 00:16:35.300
The only researchers to ever get out of that
post needed Friends in very high places.

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:37.709
Scholl, to his detriment, did not."

00:16:37.709 --> 00:16:40.949
So what exactly did Scholl do to deserve this?

00:16:40.949 --> 00:16:45.279
It is known that those who are sent to SCP-173
have made mistakes.

00:16:45.279 --> 00:16:49.629
If you disrespect your boss, you might be
reassigned to SCP-173.

00:16:49.629 --> 00:16:54.589
If you don’t follow Foundation policy, you
might be reassigned to SCP-173.

00:16:54.589 --> 00:16:59.699
If you leak information to the public, you
might be reassigned to SCP-173.

00:16:59.699 --> 00:17:03.890
If you are Jake Scholl, however, it doesn't
take quite as much.

00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:10.539
So I will pose the question once more, “What
horrible thing could Jake have done?”

00:17:10.539 --> 00:17:13.160
Could they have been plotting to help an array
of SCPs escape.

00:17:13.160 --> 00:17:18.409
Could they have been smuggling dangerous equipment
from the lab and selling it on the black market.

00:17:18.409 --> 00:17:22.539
Could they have somehow been responsible for
every casualty in Foundation history?

00:17:22.539 --> 00:17:26.949
Or could it have been something much, much
smaller.

00:17:26.949 --> 00:17:33.110
Like occasionally parking in their boss’s
favorite spot on site-217… a lot, you must

00:17:33.110 --> 00:17:36.590
understand, which doesn’t have assigned
parking.

00:17:36.590 --> 00:17:43.140
Now go check out “SCP-173 - The Complete
Story” and “SCP-173 Origin Story - How

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:49.120
173 Got to Site-19” for more tales of the
iconic SCP-173!

